{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-kxci8x"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Single source of surface tiering: one contract-declared tier per command drives CLI help, MCP tool profiles, completions, and docs together"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Four separate efforts each decide, independently, which part of pm's surface an agent sees first: tiered CLI help, MCP tool profiles capping the exposed tool count, hiding completion helper entrypoints, and hiding the internal test-runs worker. Each is correct on its own and all four answer the same question — what tier is this command in — with four mechanisms that will drift apart the moment one is edited without the others. Declare the tier once, as a field on the command contract, and derive all four surfaces from it. The tiers themselves are the decision: a core tier an agent must know to work, a standard tier it reaches for by name, a full tier that exists and is documented, and an internal tier that is reachable but never advertised. Deriving everything from one field also makes the one-screen claim testable rather than aspirational, because the core tier's rendered size is a number the gate can check."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:mcp","contracts","discoverability","simplification"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":360},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every command declares exactly one tier in contract data, and help, MCP tool profiles, shell completions, and generated docs derive visibility from that field alone; A test asserts no surface maintains its own independent visibility list; The core tier's rendered help size is asserted against the one-screen budget, making the claim mechanically checked; The first landing changes no visible surface, proven by before-and-after snapshots of help, tool lists, and completions; Changing a command's tier is a single-field change whose effect on all four surfaces appears in one regenerated snapshot diff; Package-contributed commands declare a tier through the same field, so extensions cannot bypass tiering"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Surface visibility is one declared property, not four independently maintained lists"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Four mechanisms answering one question is a drift generator; drift here means an agent sees different surfaces through CLI and MCP and cannot trust either"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Consolidates four visibility mechanisms into one contract field; the visible surfaces should be unchanged on the first landing, proven by snapshots"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Raising or lowering a command's visibility is a one-field change that updates help, MCP tools, completions, and docs at once"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-n7rr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":75},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1kxs","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"id":"pm-9k90","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"id":"pm-e2bq","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"id":"pm-lp4j","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"id":"pm-mu8m","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"},{"id":"pm-szdc","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:50.389Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"19ad34ea3a68daf5ed39bcaaa1dfa31d22685840ae73e0b4cb10b217643689bb","message":"File the tiering consolidation that keeps four visibility mechanisms from drifting apart"}
